FREE TOKEN'S ELASTICITY RESTS ON A CLEAN LAW: the complete CPU-resident expert pool remains source-of-truth; GPU residency changes performance, never correctness. Promote the analogous Bonfyre physical theorem wherever it is valid:

AUTHORITY/IDENTITY != RESIDENCY.

For any cache/accelerator representation:
- canonical semantic/derivation identity has an authoritative owner;
- fast representations (GPU slots, local caches, compiled bodies, indexes, latent projections, materialized views) are replaceable RepresentationRefs;
- eviction/resizing cannot mutate semantic truth;
- a cold miss must remain correct, only slower;
- accelerated copies carry body/representation validity and evidence, not authority;
- cache corruption/divergence must fail closed or rederive from authoritative representation.

Cross-check Stitch, BonfyreFS, vector/index surfaces, compiled formats, model state and provider caches for places that accidentally infer truth from residency/existence. The goal is one shared law, not one shared cache implementation.
